# Frontend build/dependency output. The root Dockerfile builds the backend
# `app`/`seed`/`api` images only - none of them import anything from
# frontend/, which is built by its own frontend/Dockerfile with its own
# context. Excluding these is not cosmetic: together they were ~1.15GB of
# the 1.22GB `COPY . .` layer, and because the context hash changed on
# every `next build`, each nightly `docker compose run --build` wrote a
# fresh ~1.2GB BuildKit cache entry. That filled this machine's disk and
# crash-exited Docker Desktop three times in one week (2026-10-29,
# 2026-11-02, 2026-11-07). frontend/src and the frontend config files are
# deliberately still included - they're a few hundred KB and keeping the
# directory partially present avoids surprising a future COPY.
frontend/node_modules
frontend/.next
.cache/
